course: dictionary
lesson: 11787
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. «Bel» is a good example. It can be a unit for measuring sound, a girl's name, or the name of an ancient god. The words around it show which one.
explain: «The science teacher said the drill was 90 decibels, which is nine bels.» Here the sentence is about sound, so bel is a unit for measuring loudness. Always ask: what is this sentence about? Then check that your meaning fits.
explain: «Bel and Sam walked to school together.» The capital letter and the people in the sentence show that Bel is a name. In everyday life, Bel is usually a nickname, but in science lessons the bel itself is rarely used. You will nearly always meet the decibel, which is one tenth of a bel.
fact: A bel is a unit for measuring how loud a sound is, or for comparing power levels.
fact: One bel is ten decibels, so a decibel is one tenth of a bel.
fact: «Bel» is also a name, a short form of names like Isabel or Belinda.
fact: In old stories, «Bel» was the name of an ancient Babylonian god.
fact: The unit is named after Alexander Graham Bell, who worked on the telephone.
exercise: «The engine measured 60 decibels, or six bels.» What is a bel? | *A unit for measuring how loud a sound is | A kind of musical instrument | A loud shout | A type of flower
exercise: «Bel and her sister went to the park.» In this sentence, what is Bel? | *A girl's name | A god from long ago | A type of dragon | A unit of sound
exercise: How many decibels make one bel? | One thousand | One hundred | Two | *Ten
test: «In old stories, Bel was an ancient god.» What does ancient mean here? | Very small | Very new | Very kind | *Very old
test: The unit bel is named after whom? | Thomas Edison | Alexander the Great | *Alexander Graham Bell | Isaac Newton
exam: «Ten decibels make one bel, so a decibel is what fraction of a bel?» | One half | *One tenth | One hundredth | One whole bel
